ENTRY            30987   20090919   20091224   20091223       3141
SUBENT        30987001   20090919   20091224   20091223       3141
BIB                 12         33
TITLE      Cross sections of In-113(n,n')In-113-m and
           In-113(n,2n)In-112-m+g reactions around 2 and 14
           MeV neutron energies.
AUTHOR     (Cs.M.Buczko,J.Csikai,T.Chimoye,B.W.Jimba)
INSTITUTE  (3HUNKOS)
REFERENCE  (C,91JUELIC,,656,199105)
SAMPLE     High-purity indium metal samples, 15*15*0.25 mm.
FACILITY   (CCW)
METHOD     (ACTIV)
DETECTOR   (GELI,NAICR)
           (BF3) Flux-variation in time measured by BF3
CORRECTION Corrections were carried out for the following effects:
           - Self-absorption
           - Dead time
           - Fluctuation of neutron yield as a function of time
           - Contribution of room scattered fast neutrons
           - Contribution of d-d neutrons to the (n,n') reaction
             in the 14 MeV region.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty includes statistical and
           systematic components. The principal sources of
           systematic uncertainty were:
           (ERR-1) Neutron flux determination               (2%)
           (ERR-2) Uncertainties in half-lifes              (1%)
           (ERR-3) Uncertainties in standard cross sections (1%)
             * detector efficiencies    ( Ge(Li) 1%, NaI 5%)
             * correction for D-D contribution (Subent 002) to the
             (n,n') reaction in the 14 MeV region    (<2%)
STATUS     (TABLE) Data are from Tables of 91JUELIC,,656,1991
HISTORY    (19920907C)
           (19930407U) HW.-Correction in Bib-section of subent 002
           (20090912A) SD:Updated to new date formats,lower case.
           Cosmetic changes, Common section and codes for
           err-analys were added. Source of data was changed.
ENDBIB              33
COMMON               3          3
ERR-1      ERR-2      ERR-3
PER-CENT   PER-CENT   PER-CENT
  2.          1.        1.
ENDCOMMON            3
ENDSUBENT           40
ENDENTRY             1
